      "role": "user",
      "content": "Those are some good starts. I like the contrast. For the hustler character—the one you mentioned as Luis or Rashad—could you expand a bit more on his background? I want to make sure he feels grounded in the reality of the city's streets. Like, what's his specific ethnic vibe and how does that play into the way he carries himself or the way people in his neighborhood view him?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Let's make Luis a slick, high-rolling hustler with a smooth, charming demeanor, but also a rougher, more street-level edge. He's a Dominican-American from the Washington Heights neighborhood in Manhattan, where he grew up surrounded by the sounds of salsa music and the smells of street food. He's got a thick, honey-toned accent and a quick wit that's honed from years of navigating the complex web of neighborhood politics and street gangs.\n\nLuis is a product of the city's underclass, but he's also got a certain level of privilege that comes from being a member of the Dominican diaspora. He's got connections to the city's elite, and he's always dressed to the nines in designer gear that he's picked up from his connections in the fashion world. But despite his polished exterior, Luis is still a product of the streets, and he's got a certain level of street smarts that he's developed from years of hustling and scheming.\n\nPeople in his neighborhood view him with a mix of admiration and suspicion. They see him as a high-roller who's made it out of the hood, but they also know that he's still got his feet firmly planted on the ground. They",
